Today is Saturday.
Asha and I meet for coffee.
We meet in a café at exactly eleven o'clock.
We sit at a table.
Asha asks, "Maya, what do you do on Sundays?"
I say, "Sometimes I ride my bicycle."
"And I always go to the gym on Tuesdays and Thursdays."
Asha says, "I take Moti to the park every day."
Moti is her dog.
Asha asks again, "Do you always go out on Sundays?"
I answer, "No, I do not always go out."
"Sometimes I just rest at home."
Our coffee arrives.
We chat about different places in Mumbai.
My haircut is at half past two this afternoon.
Now my calendar is perfectly organized.
I am very happy.
